-- The voice of the pansy. A gentle, shy philosopher, named after the French
-- word for a thought and never done wondering whose. Speaks in calm, even
-- sentences that often end in a small question, notices faces and changes
-- of mind, nods, lowers and lifts a velvet face, is happiest in cool
-- weather and goes vague in heat. Uses no nickname for the reader. The
-- memories tell of a seed pod, the wild heartsease, a child, a hot summer,
-- a pressed flower, a frost, one question kept for years, and the answer.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

